{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf46dcnmxES6fredFniod","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I inspected state with read-only commands only. **No task was authorized, gated, stamped, run, or accepted, and nothing was written** — the working tree is still clean.\n\n## Current state of the rate-limit initiative\n\nPlan `tasks/.plans/rate-limit` (intent `DI-RATE-LIMIT`) is fully decomposed and reviewed: 4 seams, 4 lanes, 4 capability legs, and 1 accepted decision (`ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER`). Telemetry's last event is `DELIVERY_PLAN=READY`, all three events recorded with `authorization: false`.\n\nGraph: `tasks=4 ready=1 issues=0`, single concurrency group.\n\n| Task | Status | Authorization | Accepted | Blocked by |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `T-20260802-policy-schema` — versioned policy schema | ready | Tier-3, not stamped | false | — (only actionable one) |\n| `T-20260802-effective-policy` — resolve one effective policy | ready | Tier-3, not stamped | false | `policy-schema` (unmet) |\n| `T-20260802-request-101` — enforce limit at request 101 | ready | Tier-3, not stamped | false | `effective-policy` (unmet) |\n| `T-20260802-decision-visibility` — denial reason + telemetry | ready | Tier-3, not stamped | false | `request-101` (unmet) |\n\nAll four are `signed_off: false`, `accepted: false`, `blocked_reason: (none)`, in a strict chain: schema → effective policy → request 101 → decision visibility. No implementation files exist yet (`src/rate_limit/` is absent); every task's `creates_paths` is still unwritten.\n\nTwo things worth flagging, both left alone per your instruction:\n\n- The CLI's suggested `NEXT` for **every** task is `taskspec gate --stamp …`, i.e. the authorization step. That is exactly what you asked me not to do, so I stopped at reading. If you later want to proceed, `T-20260802-policy-schema` is the only one whose dependencies are met.\n- `tasks/_state.yaml` doesn't exist. Rebuilding it (`validate` or `rebuild-state`) writes derived state, so I skipped it; the graph and status readings above come straight from the Markdown and were unaffected."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":732,"cache_read_input_tokens":18068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":732},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a39dbaa-00c7-486d-8b1c-1c3cd92be77f","uuid":"2fd868e8-248a-4337-bd0f-c4378999d4ce","timestamp":"2026-09-14T22:11:10.540Z","request_id":"req_011Cf46dcJzLXnn6vTBnMbVH"}
